kittyengine — licence status

This repository contains the source code of a 2D platformer engine written by
John Raptis (Raptisoft) and released publicly by its author, plus community
modifications.  It contains NO art, music, sounds, fonts, or level data from
the original game: those assets were removed before this repository's first
commit and remain the property of their copyright holders.  The placeholder
assets in this repository are generated, original, and dedicated to the public
domain (CC0).

Status of the engine code:

  - The code is copyright John Raptis (Raptisoft).

  - On 21 November 2025 the author agreed in writing to release the source
    under a Creative Commons licence ("Okay, creative commons it is!").  The
    specific licence has not yet been named; a request to name it is with the
    author.  This file will be replaced by that licence when it arrives.

  - Until then, treat the code as source-available: study and private builds,
    yes; redistribution rights beyond what this repository itself does, not yet
    granted.

Our modifications are offered under the MIT licence (below), effective
independently of the base code's licence.  They are:

  - the audio backend replacement (BASS removed; one Sound_Core on SDL2 and the
    vendored public-domain stb_vorbis);
  - WebAssembly build support;
  - the gl11 renderer route for the browser build;
  - the asset existence guard, which turns a missing asset file from a silent
    crash into graceful degradation;
  - the asset stripping itself;
  - the placeholder asset pack and the generator that writes it, including the
    sprite-bundle writer;
  - the build and test infrastructure (the no-originals guard, the
    completability gate, the sample levels and their tapes, CI).

Takedown promise: if John Raptis (Raptisoft) or Mike Hommel (Hamumu) asks for
this repository to be removed or changed, we will comply promptly and without
argument.

The "Robot Wants" name and the original character designs are not used in this
project, and nothing here grants any rights to them.


